1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Xenon 2: Megablast - Go / Ebitengine remake
An expert-play presentation with the game's own music and effects.

2
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:20,000
The original intro and credits
Original Amiga graphics, with independent game logic and audio replay in Go.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:33,000
A familiar Amiga presentation
The menus, scrolling backgrounds and soundtrack keep their own timing.

4
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,467
From the intro to the original menu
A normal single-player session is about to begin.

5
00:00:41,467 --> 00:00:46,633
The demonstration selects one-player mode
Cheats are disabled; loading and READY follow the normal game flow.

6
00:00:46,633 --> 00:01:02,000
The expert player takes control
Movement, shots, collisions and rewards follow the normal game rules.

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Tracking the next enemy formation
The pilot changes lanes to line up its firing bursts.

8
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Play it yourself: arrow keys, Space or Control to fire
During a normal demo, a key or touch returns control to you.

9
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:56,000
Collecting cash for the merchant
The pilot moves toward reachable bonuses left by defeated enemies.

10
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:18,000
Working through the first stage
Positioning matters as much as firepower in the narrow passages.

11
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Keeping clear of the scenery
Reverse scrolling is available when a passage is blocked.

12
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:44,233
The first section leads to the merchant
The ship keeps its remaining shield and earned cash.

13
00:02:44,233 --> 00:02:55,683
The original merchant: equipment, sales and repairs
Purchases use cash earned during the game.

14
00:02:55,683 --> 00:03:17,000
Back in the level after the merchant
The same ship continues through the second section.

15
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Different formations need different firing positions
The pilot anticipates enemy paths before opening fire.

16
00:03:40,000 --> 00:04:06,000
The original terrain and enemy-wave layouts
Display runs at 60 frames per second with separate gameplay timing.

17
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:33,000
Also available on Android
The same Go game has a virtual joystick and separate fire and dive controls.

18
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:50,000
A remake in development, with a three-level expert tour
Original resources are prepared from your own Amiga game disks.

19
00:04:50,000 --> 00:05:00,000
Xenon 2 Go | Malakh Software
